# reel's code demo, part two: moving between files. A protocol and one of its implementations side by side, linked,
# and a definition peeked in place. `mise run demos relations` records it. The files are copies in demos/code.
Import //demos/reel.reelpreset
Screen code

Output //docs/media/relations.mp4
Output //docs/media/relations.gif
Set Viewport 1100x620
Set FontSize 18
Intro@crossfade,ease-out,600ms square ? "reel" "Between files" : 2s
Outro@fade,800ms square ? "Recorded with reel" "brew install --cask mpdreamz/tap/reel" : 2s

Code code/Synthesizer.swift
Say "A code walkthrough moves between files. Here's a protocol,"
Code@slide-left,ease-in-out,600ms code/Voicebox.swift at "struct Voicebox"
Say "and here's what implements it."
Code@crossfade code/Synthesizer.swift
Split code/Voicebox.swift at "struct Voicebox"
Say "Side by side,"
Link "protocol Synthesizer" -> "struct Voicebox: Synthesizer" "conforms to"
Link "func speak" -> "func speak" "implements"
Say "with the relations drawn between them, declared in the reel."
Link off
Go "profileID()"
Peek "profileID()" code/Voicebox.swift at "func profileID"
Say "And a definition can open right where it's used."
Peek off
Split off
Sleep 1s
